      "assistant": "There's nothing worse than mushy mashed potatoes! Here's how to tell when boiled potatoes are perfectly ready to mash, broken down into a few methods:\n\n**1. The Tooth Test (The Best Method!)**\n\n* **The Idea:** This is the gold standard. It's all about feeling for resistance.\n* **How to Do It:**  Carefully use a fork to pierce a potato.  Press gently.  If the fork slides in and out with *no* resistance, they're not done. If there's a little give, but it's still firm, they're getting there.  When the fork slides in and out easily with a slight *spring*, they're ready.\n* **Don't:** Don't rely on just timing.  Potatoes vary in size and thickness, so cooking times are just a guideline.\n\n**2. Visual Cues (Good as a Supplement)**\n\n* **Skin Peeling:** The skin should slip off easily. If you have to really tug and strain, they need more time.\n* **Color:** They should be a pale, even yellow.  If they're still very white, they're undercooked.  If they",
